{
  "id": "ss.terrain.web-span",
  "name": "Silk span (SS)",
  "description": "Silk strung between two trunks, authored along +x and stretched to whatever gap the game found one in. Six loaded lines drawn in five segments each so the droop is a curve rather than a tent, with a tangle of cross-links hung under them at every angle but square, drop lines that end in nothing, and the whole thing beaded \u2014 which is what a web between two trees actually looks like. It thickens at both ends where it is tied on, the part that says anchored rather than floating. `torn` is what is left after a body has been through the middle of it.",
